module

public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.NormalConeFibreConstructions
import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.SchemeNearPointNormalCone

/-! # The normal cone at a Hilbert--Samuel near point

Source: ILO, Exposé VIII 2.3.13, p.94; Cossart--Jannsen--Saito, March 2009 preprint,
Theorems 2.3 and 2.14 (blueprint: lem-trf-hilbert-samuel-near-normal-cone).
The fibre comparison below is specified on every Rees monomial, so its point is the
original blowup point, with no arbitrary identification of projective schemes.
-/

@[expose] public section
set_option autoImplicit false

universe u
open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TensorProduct

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.HilbertSamuel

/-- A constant smooth centre is normally flat. At a near point its exceptional fibre
has a positive-dimensional linear factor whose projectivization contains that point.
Source: ILO VIII 2.3.13, p.94; CJS Theorems 2.3 and 2.14.
(blueprint: lem-trf-hilbert-samuel-near-normal-cone).

Proof, following the node's ten steps:
1. Work in an affine neighbourhood where the ambient embedding is closed. Finite type
   gives Noetherianity. The conormal stalk formula identifies A with the centre's local
   ring; smoothness makes A regular and a domain. Remove other components of the centre
   and shrink into its constant-H neighbourhood.
2. The dimension/transcendence-degree formula at the generic point eta of that component
   gives t_eta = t_x + dim A. Constancy and injectivity of inclusive summation therefore
   give h_R = Lambda^(dim A) h_(R_I).
3. Apply lem-trf-bennett-normal-flat-numerical-criterion to obtain A-flatness of G.
4. The transcendence-degree tower formula converts H_y = H_x to the raw near equality
   Lambda^(trdeg_k k(y)) h_y = h_R, without replacing either point by a closed point.
5. Localize the Rees algebra, then base change Proj to k. In degree n, both the fibre and
   k tensor_A G_n are I^n/m I^n, since I^(n+1) is contained in m I^n. Their products agree
   on representatives. This gives precisely the monomial-specified pullback below.
6. A minimal prime containing I would equal I. Reduced localization is then a field;
   torsion-freeness of the flat G over the domain A gives I = I^2. Nakayama gives I = 0,
   making Proj empty, contrary to the specified point. Thus the centre contains no component.
7. Finite generators of I give a standard graded presentation P = k[Z] onto S with kernel K.
   Apply lem-trf-near-point-additive-symmetry to obtain a proper homogeneous additive
   subgroup ideal L contained in the point's inverse-image prime, with K contained in L
   and g(Z+W) in K(Z)+L(W) for g in K.
8. In characteristic zero L is generated by L_1: a least-degree element after quotienting
   by L_1 has all partial derivatives zero by the (1,r-1) component of its comultiplication;
   Euler's identity contradicts its positive degree. Choose coordinates L=(U), with at
   least one remaining T because the point's prime is relevant.
9. Taylor coefficients in the T variables preserve K; evaluation at T=0 also preserves K.
   Hence K=J[T] for J=K intersect k[U], by comparing each coefficient.
10. Take B=k[U]/J with its standard grading. Then S=B[T], and containment of L in the
    point's prime is exactly containment of B_+. Surjective graded Proj functoriality
    identifies its zero locus with Proj k[T]. All assertions concern scheme points. -/
theorem near_normal_cone {X C P : Scheme.{u}}
    (p : P ⟶ Spec (.of (ULift.{u} ℚ))) (i : X ⟶ P) (c : C ⟶ X)
    [Smooth p] [IsImmersion i] [IsReduced X]
    [LocallyOfFiniteType (i ≫ p)] [QuasiCompact (i ≫ p)]
    [IsClosedImmersion c] [Smooth (c ≫ i ≫ p)]
    (hconstant : IsLocallyConstant (fun z : C ↦ function (i ≫ p) (c z)))
    (z : C) (y : c.ker.blowup) (hy : c.ker.blowupMap y = c z)
    (hnear : function (c.ker.blowupMap ≫ i ≫ p) y = function (i ≫ p) (c z)) :
    Module.Flat (X.presheaf.stalk (c z) ⧸ centerStalkIdeal c z)
      (Ideal.associatedGraded (centerStalkIdeal c z)) ∧
    ∃ (_ : GradedAlgebra (normalFibreGrade c z))
      (φ : reesGrading (centerStalkIdeal c z) →+*ᵍ normalFibreGrade c z)
      (hirr : HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant (normalFibreGrade c z) ≤
        (HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant (reesGrading (centerStalkIdeal c z))).map φ),
      (∀ (n : ℕ) (a : (centerStalkIdeal c z ^ n : Ideal (X.presheaf.stalk (c z)))),
        φ (reesMonomial (centerStalkIdeal c z) a.val a.property) =
          (1 : X.residueField (c z)) ⊗ₜ[X.presheaf.stalk (c z) ⧸ centerStalkIdeal c z]
            DirectSum.of (Ideal.associatedGradedPiece (centerStalkIdeal c z)) n
              (Submodule.Quotient.mk a)) ∧
      ∃ (U : X.affineOpens) (hx : c z ∈ U.1)
        (hI : (c.ker.ideal U).map (X.presheaf.germ U.1 (c z) hx).hom = centerStalkIdeal c z),
        IsPullback
          (Proj.map φ hirr ≫
            AffineBlowup.hom (X.presheaf.germ U.1 (c z) hx).hom hI ≫ c.ker.blowupι U)
          (Proj.toSpecOfAlgebra (normalFibreGrade c z)) c.ker.blowupMap
          (X.fromSpecResidueField (c z)) ∧
        ∃ (t : Proj (normalFibreGrade c z)) (B : Type u) (_ : CommRing B)
          (_ : Algebra (X.residueField (c z)) B)
          (𝓑 : ℕ → Submodule (X.residueField (c z)) B)
          (_ : GradedAlgebra 𝓑) (_ : GradedAlgebra.IsStandard 𝓑)
          (r : ℕ) (e : normalFibre c z ≃ₐ[X.residueField (c z)] MvPolynomial (Fin r) B),
          1 ≤ r ∧
          (∀ (n : ℕ) (s : normalFibre c z),
            s ∈ normalFibreGrade c z n ↔ e s ∈ normalPolynomialGrade 𝓑 r n) ∧
          (Proj.map φ hirr ≫
            AffineBlowup.hom (X.presheaf.germ U.1 (c z) hx).hom hI ≫ c.ker.blowupι U) t = y ∧
          ∀ (n : ℕ), 0 < n → ∀ b ∈ 𝓑 n,
            e.symm (MvPolynomial.C b) ∈ t.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal := by
  exact near_normal_cone_nonreduced p i c hconstant z y hy hnear

end AlgebraicGeometry.HilbertSamuel
